+Aegis Enterprise Gate — canonical end‑to‑end acceptance run
+
+Purpose
+- A single, automatable acceptance run that proves Aegis mitigations for the highest risks:
+  secure aggregation (vetted), client attestation + mTLS, multi‑node DeepSpeed stability, SBOM blocking policies, GPU power calibration for carbon accounting, and signed auditor bundle creation.
+
+Preconditions
+- Secrets configured: COSIGN_KMS_URI, REKOR_SERVER, S3_UPLOAD, REDIS_URL, VAULT_ADDR, VAULT_TOKEN.
+- Images built & pushed to CONTAINER_REGISTRY.
+- Cluster context set and operator has admin rights.
+- cert-manager available in the cluster (or cluster can accept self-signed certs).
+
+High level steps (automatable, also provided as one-click script ops/runbooks/aegis_enterprise_gate.sh)
+1) CI & Image Signing gating
+   - Ensure GitHub Actions for pre-deploy checks are enabled (pre_deploy_checks.yml).
+   - Verify that images used in manifests are cosign-signed.
+2) Deploy webhooks (cert-manager + image-signature webhook + carbon webhook)
+   - Deploy ClusterIssuer and Certificate for webhooks.
+   - Patch CA bundle into ValidatingWebhookConfiguration.
+3) Secure aggregation & attestation
+   - Install vetted secure-aggregation library on the platform (see ops/fl/secure_agg_install_instructions.md).
+   - Provision Vault PKI role and issue per-client certs for FL clients (ops/fl/attestation/vault_pki_setup.sh).
+   - Enforce mTLS for FL ingress/load‑balancer.
+4) FL round with DP clients
+   - Start FL server, run 3 Opacus clients, trigger aggregation, run enhanced validator.
+   - Verify validator returns success and evidence bundle is cosign-signed.
+5) DeepSpeed multi-node validation
+   - Run ops/ml/validation/deepspeed_full_test.sh with NUM_NODES and GPUS_PER_NODE.
+   - Verify checkpoint integrity with verify_zero_checkpoints.py.
+6) Serving validation
+   - Run triton_load_test.py and vllm_load_test.py against deployed serving endpoints.
+7) SBOM enforcement & CVE blocking
+   - Run SBOM generation (syft) & grype scanning for all images; block on HIGH/CRITICAL CVEs.
+8) GPU power calibration & carbon exporter
+   - Run ops/telemetry/pdu_ipmi_compare.py to compute calibration factor.
+   - Apply calibration to cluster ConfigMap (ops/telemetry/calibration_apply_configmap.sh).
+   - Re-run a sample job and use job_carbon_exporter to produce calibrated CO2e artifact.
+9) Auditor bundle
+   - Assemble SBOMs, evidence bundles, validation reports into a signed auditor bundle (ops/compliance/prepare_audit_bundle_and_rekor.sh).
+   - Upload to S3 and create Rekor entry (if rekor-cli present).
+
+Exit criteria (must all pass)
+- Image signature verification: all images used in manifests are cosign-signed by authorized KMS key.
+- Secure aggregation: library integrated and secagg smoke test passes.
+- Attestation: clients issued certificates from Vault PKI and server enforces mTLS.
+- FL validator: aggregated model passes holdout validation; outliers within limits.
+- DeepSpeed: NCCL job finishes without errors and ZeRO checkpoint verification passes.
+- SBOM: grype scan returns no HIGH/CRITICAL vulns for production images.
+- Calibration: calibration file applied and job_carbon_exporter produces calibrated measured_power_w in artifact.
+- Auditor bundle: signed via cosign and uploaded to S3; Rekor entry present.
+
+If any step fails, collect logs, bundle artifacts, and open an incident as per docs/incidents/incident_playbook.md.
+
