+Secure aggregation installation & crypto review instructions
+
+Recommended library choices
+- Google secagg reference implementation (https://github.com/google/secagg) — reference, requires build and Python bindings.
+- CrypTen (https://crypten.ai) — includes secure MPC and some aggregation primitives.
+- If you choose a commercial or audited implementation, request its audit artifacts before integration.
+
+Install (example for secagg reference):
+1. Clone and build the secagg reference repo in a secure build environment:
+   git clone https://github.com/google/secagg.git /opt/secagg
+   Follow the repo README to build Python bindings.
+2. Ensure the built package is importable by Python processes that run FL server/client (install to virtualenv or container).
+3. Run ops/fl/tests/secagg_integration_test.py to validate integration.
+
+Crypto review checklist
+- Ensure the implementation's spec and proofs are available.
+- Run >100-client simulations and dropout scenarios.
+- Review key exchange ephemeral key rotation and replay protections.
+- Engage external cryptographer for code audit and threat model review.
+
